{"meta":{"dataset":"eeoc-charges","title":"Employment discrimination charges to the EEOC, by state and basis, FY 2009 to FY 2025","version":"1.0.0","doi":"10.5281/zenodo.23733005","doiUrl":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23733005","conceptDoi":"10.5281/zenodo.23733004","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","attribution":"Source: Probative, Employment discrimination charges to the EEOC, by state and basis, FY 2009 to FY 2025, version 1.0.0, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23733005, licensed CC BY 4.0.","citation":"Probative. (2026). Employment discrimination charges to the EEOC, by state and basis, FY 2009 to FY 2025 (Version 1.0.0) [Data set]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23733005","disclaimer":"Not legal advice. These are counts of charges received by the EEOC, kept for marketing planning. A charge is an allegation, not a finding of discrimination, and the counts leave out charges filed only with state and local agencies. Deadlines and rights are for your own counsel.","notice":"Probative is a marketing firm, not a law firm; not legal advice.","lastChecked":"2026-10-27","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/eeoc-charges/index.json","humanUrl":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/eeoc-charges/","statusCodes":{"P":"primary source","S":"secondary source","D":"ABA model default","U":"open question"}},"summary":"Charges of workplace discrimination received by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission (EEOC), by state, DC, Puerto Rico and territory, fiscal year and basis (race, sex, national origin, religion, color, retaliation, age, disability, equal pay, genetic information and pregnancy under the Pregnant Workers Fairness Act), from the EEOC's Tables E1b and E1a. One record per jurisdiction and basis for the latest fiscal year, each with its count, its share of the state's charges, the rate per 100,000 private-sector workers (BLS Quarterly Census of Employment and Wages, from fiscal year 2014) and the whole